{"id":"79d5c9379600751b189d6e56a2fce3b3c0ddaae1","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"79d5c9379600751b189d6e56a2fce3b3c0ddaae1","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/models/pooling_models/README.md","lines":["@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ enabling the corresponding APIs."," | Classification Usages       | `LLM.classify(...)` | `classify`                        | `cross-encoder` (see note) | linear classifier        |"," | Embedding Usages            | `LLM.embed(...)`    | `embed`                           | `bi-encoder`               | cosine similarity        |"," | Token Classification Usages | N/A                 | `token_classify`                  | N/A                        | N/A                      |","-| Token Embedding Usages      | N/A                 | `token_embed`                     | `late-interaction`         | late interaction(MaxSim) |","+| Token Embedding Usages      | `LLM.embed(...)`    | `token_embed`                     | `late-interaction`         | late interaction(MaxSim) |"," | Reward Usages               | N/A                 | `classify` & `token_classify`     | N/A                        | N/A                      |"," | Scoring Usages              | `LLM.score(...)`    | N/A                               | N/A                        | N/A                      |"," | Plugins Usages              | N/A                 | `plugin`                          | N/A                        | N/A                      |","@@ -146,9 +146,9 @@ For more information about `LLM.classify`, see [this page](classify.md#offline-i"," "," ### `LLM.embed`"," ","-The [embed][vllm.LLM.embed] method outputs an embedding vector for each prompt.","+The [embed][vllm.LLM.embed] method outputs one embedding vector per prompt with the `embed` task, or a matrix of token vectors with the `token_embed` task. Eligible token embedding models also support [late chunking](token_embed.md#fixed-length-late-chunking) through this method."," It is primarily designed for [embedding models](embed.md).","-For more information about `LLM.embed`, see [this page](embed.md#offline-inference).","+For more information about `LLM.embed`, see the [sequence embedding](embed.md#offline-inference) and [token embedding](token_embed.md#offline-inference) guides."," "," ### `LLM.score`"," ","@@ -178,8 +178,9 @@ print(f\"Data: {data!r}\")"," Our online Server provides endpoints that correspond to the offline APIs:"," "," - Corresponding to `LLM.embed`:","-    - [Cohere Embed API](embed.md#cohere-embed-api) (`/v2/embed`)","+    - [Cohere Embed API](embed.md#cohere-embed-api) (`/v2/embed`) for the `embed` task","     - [OpenAI-compatible Embeddings API](embed.md#openai-compatible-embeddings-api) (`/v1/embeddings`)","+    - [Token Embeddings API](token_embed.md#online-serving) (`/v1/embeddings`) for the `token_embed` task, returning token or chunk vectors as a vLLM extension"," - Corresponding to `LLM.classify`:","     - [Classification API](classify.md#online-serving)(`/classify`)"," - Corresponding to `LLM.score`:"],"additions":5,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/models/pooling_models/token_embed.md","lines":["@@ -5,9 +5,11 @@"," - Model Usage: Token classification models"," - Pooling Tasks: `token_embed`"," - Offline APIs:","+    - `LLM.embed(...)` with the `token_embed` pooling task","     - `LLM.encode(..., pooling_task=\"token_embed\")`"," - Online APIs:","     - Pooling API (`/pooling`)","+    - Embedding API (`/v1/embeddings`), with optional [late chunking](#online-late-chunking)"," "," The difference between the (sequence) embedding task and the token embedding task is that (sequence) embedding outputs one embedding for each sequence, while token embedding outputs an embedding for each token."," ","@@ -98,7 +100,7 @@ The following [pooling parameters][vllm.PoolingParams] are supported."," "," The [encode][vllm.entrypoints.pooling.offline.PoolingOfflineMixin.encode] method is available to all pooling models in vLLM."," ","-Set `pooling_task=\"token_embed\"` when using `LLM.encode` for token embedding Models:","+Set `pooling_task=\"token_embed\"` when using `LLM.encode` for token embedding models:"," "," ```python"," from vllm import LLM","@@ -110,19 +112,32 @@ data = output.outputs.data"," print(f\"Data: {data!r}\")"," ```"," ","+### `LLM.embed`","+","+The [embed][vllm.entrypoints.pooling.offline.PoolingOfflineMixin.embed] method uses the model's configured pooling task. For `token_embed`, it returns a `PoolingRequestOutput` per input, with a token-vector matrix in `outputs.data`. Ordinary `embed` models keep returning `EmbeddingRequestOutput` with one vector in `outputs.embedding`.","+","+```python","+from vllm import LLM","+","+llm = LLM(model=\"answerdotai/answerai-colbert-small-v1\", runner=\"pooling\")","+(output,) = llm.embed(\"Hello, my name is\")","+","+data = output.outputs.data","+print(f\"Data: {data!r}\")","+```","+"," ### Fixed-length late chunking"," "," Late chunking encodes the full input before averaging contextual token representations within each chunk. The chunk means pass through the model's embedding head, including its projection and optional normalization."," ","-This mode is currently available through the offline `LLM.encode` API for plain-text input. With an instance configured for `token_embed`, enable it per request:","+With an instance configured for `token_embed`, enable late chunking per request through `LLM.embed` for plain-text input:"," "," ```python"," from vllm import PoolingParams"," from vllm.pooling_params import LateChunkingParams"," ","-outputs = llm.encode(","+outputs = llm.embed(","     [document],","-    pooling_task=\"token_embed\",","     pooling_params=PoolingParams(","         late_chunking_params=LateChunkingParams(chunk_size=256)","     ),","@@ -131,6 +146,8 @@ vectors = outputs[0].outputs.data  # [num_chunks, embedding_dimension]"," chunks = outputs[0].late_chunking.chunks"," ```"," ","+To use `LLM.encode` instead, pass the same pooling parameters and set `pooling_task=\"token_embed\"`.","+"," For `N` model-input tokens and chunk size `C`, the output contains `ceil(N / C)` vectors. The last chunk uses its actual length. Special tokens and instruction prefixes count toward both chunk boundaries and means. Omitting `late_chunking_params` preserves ordinary token embeddings."," "," Each vector row corresponds to one entry in `chunks`. Its `token_range` and `char_range` are zero-based, half-open ranges. Character ranges index the submitted Python string; use `document[start:end]` to retrieve the source text. A chunk containing only special tokens has `char_range=None`.","@@ -164,7 +181,72 @@ print(f\"Score: {score}\")"," "," ## Online Serving"," ","-Please refer to the [Pooling API](README.md#pooling-api) and use `\"task\":\"token_embed\"`.","+### Embedding API","+","+On a server configured for `token_embed`, `/v1/embeddings` returns token vectors by default and chunk vectors when `late_chunking_params` is provided.","+","+#### Online late chunking","+","+Start a token embedding server, for example:","+","+```bash","+vllm serve intfloat/multilingual-e5-small \\","+    --runner pooling --pooler-config.task token_embed --max-model-len 512","+```","+","+Set `late_chunking_params.chunk_size` to a positive integer less than `2**63`:","+","+```bash","+curl http://localhost:8000/v1/embeddings \\","+    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\","+    -d '{","+      \"model\": \"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small\",","+      \"input\": \"passage: Berlin has many museums. They display art from around the world.\",","+      \"late_chunking_params\": {\"chunk_size\": 16},","+      \"encoding_format\": \"float\"","+    }'","+```","+","+Each response item contains `embedding`, a `[num_chunks, embedding_dimension]` matrix, and `late_chunking`, with these fields:","+","+| Field | Meaning |","+| --- | --- |","+| `strategy` | `\"fixed_tokens\"` |","+| `chunk_size` | Requested number of model-input tokens per chunk |","+| `input_tokens` | Number of tokens in this document, including special tokens |","+| `chunks` | One entry per vector row, containing `token_range` and `char_range` |","+","+Ranges have the same semantics as the offline API. JSON represents them as two-element arrays; `char_range` is `null` for a special-token-only chunk. Character indices count Unicode code points, so clients using UTF-16 string indices must convert them before slicing.","+","+Use a string or a nonempty list of strings as `input`. A batch shares one chunk size, returns one item per document in input order, and counts input tokens once in `usage`. Values of `chunk_size` larger than the input token count produce one chunk.","+","+Omit `late_chunking_params` or set it to `null` to return ordinary token vectors through the same endpoint. Each item then contains a token-vector matrix in `embedding` and omits `late_chunking`. This mode also accepts token IDs. With late chunking enabled, input must be plain text and must not request truncation or padding, because source ranges refer to the complete submitted text. Only `encoding_format=\"float\"` is supported; chat messages and `dimensions` are unsupported by this endpoint.","+","+The matrix-valued `embedding` and `late_chunking` fields are a vLLM extension, not the standard OpenAI embedding response. Use an HTTP client that handles this format. Ordinary `embed` servers keep their existing response format; they do not enable late chunking and may ignore an unrecognized `late_chunking_params` field. Cohere `/v2/embed`, the batch API, and `/invocations` are not extended with late chunking.","+","+#### Retrieve source text from chunk vectors","+","+The [retrieval example](../../../examples/pooling/token_embed/late_chunking_retrieval_online.py) uses the server above to:","+","+1. Encode documents with E5's `passage:` prefix and request contextual chunks.","+2. Build an in-memory index containing vectors, document IDs, chunk indices and source ranges.","+3. Encode a question with the `query:` prefix, using one chunk covering the whole query.","+4. Rank stored vectors by cosine similarity and print the matching source excerpts.","+","+```bash","+python examples/pooling/token_embed/late_chunking_retrieval_online.py \\","+    --chunk-size 16 --query \"Which city has museums with art collections?\"","+```","+","+Add `--index-path late_chunking_index.json` to save the index. The example creates no index file by default.","+","+For E5, one chunk covering the complete query produces its mean-pooled sequence embedding. Other models may require a different query head. Keep the model revision, prefixes, projection and normalization consistent between indexing and querying.","+","+Source ranges refer to the exact submitted text, including the prefix. The example excludes special-token-only chunks from retrieval. Fixed token boundaries may split sentences; late chunking does not guarantee better retrieval on every dataset.","+","+### Pooling API","+","+Use the [Pooling API](README.md#pooling-api) with `\"task\": \"token_embed\"` to return token vectors. The Pooling API does not support late chunking."," "," ## More examples"," "],"additions":87,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"examples/pooling/token_embed/late_chunking_offline.py","lines":["@@ -43,9 +43,8 @@ def main(args: Namespace):","         \"passage: Kyoto is a city in Japan. Its historic temples attract visitors \"","         \"throughout the year.\",","     ]","-    outputs = llm.encode(","+    outputs = llm.embed(","         documents,","-        pooling_task=\"token_embed\",","         pooling_params=pooling_params,","     )"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"examples/pooling/token_embed/late_chunking_retrieval_online.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+","+\"\"\"Index contextual chunks and retrieve source excerpts with multilingual E5.","+","+Start the server with:","+    vllm serve intfloat/multilingual-e5-small --runner pooling \\","+        --pooler-config.task token_embed --max-model-len 512","+","+Then run this file to search an in-memory index. Use --index-path to save it.","+\"\"\"","+","+import argparse","+import json","+from pathlib import Path","+","+import numpy as np","+import requests","+","+","+def encode(session, args, texts, chunk_size):","+    response = session.post(","+        f\"{args.url.rstrip('/')}/v1/embeddings\",","+        json={","+            \"model\": args.model,","+            \"input\": texts,","+            \"encoding_format\": \"float\",","+            \"use_activation\": True,","+            \"late_chunking_params\": {\"chunk_size\": chunk_size},","+        },","+        timeout=120,","+    )","+    response.raise_for_status()","+    return response.json()[\"data\"]","+","+","+def main(args):","+    # Ranges refer to these exact submitted strings, including the E5 prefix.","+    documents = {","+        \"berlin\": \"passage: Berlin is the capital of Germany. The city has many \"","+        \"museums. They display art and historical collections from around the world.\",","+        \"kyoto\": \"passage: Kyoto is a city in Japan. Its historic temples attract \"","+        \"visitors throughout the year.\",","+        \"storage\": \"passage: Database backups protect data from accidental loss. \"","+        \"They should be tested regularly to ensure that recovery works.\",","+    }","+    chunks = []","+    with requests.Session() as session:","+        outputs = encode(session, args, list(documents.values()), args.chunk_size)","+        for doc_id, output in zip(documents, outputs):","+            for index, (vector, chunk) in enumerate(","+                zip(output[\"embedding\"], output[\"late_chunking\"][\"chunks\"])","+            ):","+                if chunk[\"char_range\"] is None:","+                    continue  # No source text to retrieve for special-only chunks.","+                chunks.append(","+                    {","+                        \"document_id\": doc_id,","+                        \"chunk_index\": index,","+                        \"vector\": vector,","+                        **chunk,","+                    }","+                )","+","+        # E5 uses mean pooling. One chunk covering the query gives its sequence","+        # embedding, with the same model, head and normalization as the documents.","+        # The server rejects queries longer than its 512-token context window.","+        query = encode(session, args, [f\"query: {args.query}\"], chunk_size=512)[0]","+        (query_embedding,) = query[\"embedding\"]","+        query_vector = np.asarray(query_embedding, dtype=np.float32)","+","+    if args.index_path is not None:","+        args.index_path.write_text(","+            json.dumps(","+                {","+                    \"model\": args.model,","+                    \"chunk_size\": args.chunk_size,","+                    \"documents\": documents,","+                    \"chunks\": chunks,","+                },","+                ensure_ascii=False,","+            ),","+            encoding=\"utf-8\",","+        )","+        print(f\"Saved {len(chunks)} chunks to {args.index_path}\")","+    vectors = np.asarray([chunk[\"vector\"] for chunk in chunks], dtype=np.float32)","+    scores = vectors @ query_vector  # Cosine similarity for normalized vectors.","+    for index in np.argsort(-scores)[: args.top_k]:","+        chunk = chunks[index]","+        start, end = chunk[\"char_range\"]","+        excerpt = documents[chunk[\"document_id\"]][start:end]","+        print(","+            f\"{scores[index]:.4f} {chunk['document_id']} \"","+            f\"chunk {chunk['chunk_index']}: {excerpt!r}\"","+        )","+","+","+if __name__ == \"__main__\":","+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)","+    parser.add_argument(\"--url\", default=\"http://localhost:8000\")","+    parser.add_argument(\"--model\", default=\"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small\")","+    parser.add_argument(\"--chunk-size\", type=int, default=16)","+    parser.add_argument(","+        \"--query\", default=\"Which city has museums with art collections?\"","+    )","+    parser.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=3)","+    parser.add_argument(","+        \"--index-path\", type=Path, help=\"Optionally save the index as JSON.\"","+    )","+    main(parser.parse_args())"],"additions":110,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/pooling/embed/test_offline.py","lines":["@@ -58,10 +58,10 @@ def test_list_prompts(llm: LLM):","     prompts: list[PromptType] = [prompt, prompt_token_ids]","     outputs = llm.embed(prompts, use_tqdm=False)","     assert len(outputs) == 2","-    for i in range(len(outputs)):","-        assert isinstance(outputs[i], EmbeddingRequestOutput)","-        assert outputs[i].prompt_token_ids == prompt_token_ids","-        assert len(outputs[i].outputs.embedding) == embedding_size","+    for output in outputs:","+        assert isinstance(output, EmbeddingRequestOutput)","+        assert output.prompt_token_ids == prompt_token_ids","+        assert len(output.outputs.embedding) == embedding_size"," "," "," @pytest.mark.skip_global_cleanup","@@ -72,7 +72,11 @@ def get_outputs(normalize):","             pooling_params=PoolingParams(use_activation=normalize),","             use_tqdm=False,","         )","-        return torch.tensor([x.outputs.embedding for x in outputs])","+        embeddings = []","+        for output in outputs:","+            assert isinstance(output, EmbeddingRequestOutput)","+            embeddings.append(output.outputs.embedding)","+        return torch.tensor(embeddings)"," ","     default = get_outputs(normalize=None)","     w_normal = get_outputs(normalize=True)"],"additions":9,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/pooling/test_factories.py","lines":["@@ -1,16 +1,25 @@"," # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0"," # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"," ","+from types import SimpleNamespace"," from unittest.mock import MagicMock"," "," import pytest","+from fastapi import FastAPI","+from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse","+from fastapi.testclient import TestClient"," ","+from vllm import PoolingParams"," from vllm.entrypoints.pooling import factories"," from vllm.entrypoints.pooling.factories import init_pooling_io_processors"," from vllm.entrypoints.pooling.pooling.io_processor import (","     PluginWithIOProcessorPlugins,","     UnsupportedCombinedTaskIOProcessor,"," )","+from vllm.entrypoints.pooling.token_embed.serving import ServingTokenEmbedding","+from vllm.entrypoints.serve.exception_handling.register import init_exception_handler","+from vllm.exceptions import VLLMValidationError","+from vllm.pooling_params import LateChunkingParams"," "," "," def _bge_m3_config(io_processor_plugin=None):","@@ -92,3 +101,93 @@ def test_combined_task_plain_pooling_request_has_actionable_error(monkeypatch):","     io_processor = serving.get_io_processor(request)","     with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"plugin request with a 'data' field\"):","         io_processor.create_pooling_params(request)","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"task\", [\"embed\", \"token_embed\"])","+def test_embedding_route_validates_the_configured_task(task):","+    \"\"\"Invalid chunk requests must never fall back to the ordinary schema.\"\"\"","+    app = FastAPI()","+    app.state.args = SimpleNamespace(log_error_stack=False)","+    init_exception_handler(app)","+    model_config = MagicMock()","+    model_config.get_pooling_task.return_value = task","+    model_config.is_cross_encoder = False","+    factories.register_pooling_api_routers(app, (\"embed\", \"token_embed\"), model_config)","+    received = []","+","+    async def handle(request, raw_request):","+        received.append(request)","+        return JSONResponse({\"task\": task})","+","+    if task == \"token_embed\":","+        app.state.serving_token_embedding = handle","+    else:","+        app.state.serving_embedding = handle","+","+    with TestClient(app) as client:","+        if task == \"embed\":","+            assert client.post(\"/v1/embeddings\", json={\"input\": \"text\"}).json() == {","+                \"task\": \"embed\"","+            }","+            assert client.post(\"/v2/embed\", json={\"texts\": [\"text\"]}).status_code == 200","+            return","+","+        assert client.post(\"/v2/embed\", json={\"texts\": [\"text\"]}).status_code == 404","+        bad_requests: list[dict[str, object]] = [","+            {\"late_chunking_params\": {}},","+            {\"late_chunking_params\": {\"chunk_size\": 2, \"metadata\": {}}},","+            {\"encoding_format\": \"base64\"},","+            {\"dimensions\": 128},","+        ]","+        bad_requests.extend(","+            {\"late_chunking_params\": {\"chunk_size\": value}}","+            for value in (0, -1, True, 1.5, \"2\", 2**63, 2**64)","+        )","+        for overrides in bad_requests:","+            body: dict[str, object] = {\"input\": \"text\", **overrides}","+            if \"late_chunking_params\" not in overrides and overrides:","+                body[\"late_chunking_params\"] = {\"chunk_size\": 2}","+            response = client.post(\"/v1/embeddings\", json=body)","+            assert response.status_code == 400, response.text","+        assert not received","+","+        for body in (","+            {\"input\": \"text\"},","+            {\"input\": [\"text\", \"another text\"], \"late_chunking_params\": None},","+            {\"input\": [1, 2]},","+        ):","+            response = client.post(\"/v1/embeddings\", json=body)","+            assert response.json() == {\"task\": \"token_embed\"}","+            params = received[-1].to_pooling_params()","+            assert params.task == \"token_embed\"","+            assert params.late_chunking_params is None","+","+        for chunk_size in (1, 1024, 2**63 - 1):","+            response = client.post(","+                \"/v1/embeddings\",","+                json={","+                    \"input\": \"text\",","+                    \"late_chunking_params\": {\"chunk_size\": chunk_size},","+                },","+            )","+            assert response.json() == {\"task\": \"token_embed\"}","+            params = received[-1].to_pooling_params()","+            assert params.task == \"token_embed\"","+            assert params.late_chunking_params.chunk_size == chunk_size","+","+","+def test_token_embedding_keeps_model_specific_chunking_rejection():","+    vllm_config, renderer, chat_template_config = _bge_m3_config()","+    vllm_config.model_config.get_pooling_task.return_value = \"token_embed\"","+    vllm_config.model_config.architecture = \"JinaForRanking\"","+    serving = object.__new__(ServingTokenEmbedding)","+    processor = serving.init_io_processor(","+        vllm_config=vllm_config,","+        renderer=renderer,","+        chat_template_config=chat_template_config,","+    )","+    with pytest.raises(VLLMValidationError, match=\"JinaForRanking.*late chunking\"):","+        processor.render(","+            {\"params\": PoolingParams(late_chunking_params=LateChunkingParams(2))}","+        )","+    renderer.render_cmpl.assert_not_called()"],"additions":99,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/pooling/token_embed/test_late_chunking.py","lines":["rename from tests/entrypoints/pooling/test_late_chunking.py","rename to tests/entrypoints/pooling/token_embed/test_late_chunking.py","@@ -1,12 +1,15 @@"," # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0"," # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"," ","+import asyncio","+import json"," from types import SimpleNamespace"," from unittest import mock"," from unittest.mock import Mock"," "," import pytest"," import torch","+from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse, ORJSONResponse"," "